"></circle><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"80\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#1A73E8\" opacity=\"1\"></circle><circle cx=\"134\" cy=\"80\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"158\" cy=\"80\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"182\" cy=\"80\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"206\" cy=\"80\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"80\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"102\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"102\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"62\" cy=\"102\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"86\" cy=\"102\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"102\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"134\" cy=\"102\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#1A73E8\" opacity=\"1\"></circle><circle cx=\"158\" cy=\"102\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"182\" cy=\"102\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"206\" cy=\"102\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"102\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"124\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"124\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"62\" cy=\"124\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"86\" cy=\"124\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"124\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"134\" cy=\"124\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"158\" cy=\"124\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#1A73E8\" opacity=\"1\"></circle><circle cx=\"182\" cy=\"124\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"206\" cy=\"124\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"124\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"146\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"146\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"62\" cy=\"146\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"86\" cy=\"146\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"146\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"134\" cy=\"146\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"158\" cy=\"146\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"182\" cy=\"146\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#1A73E8\" opacity=\"1\"></circle><circle cx=\"206\" cy=\"146\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"146\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"168\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"168\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"62\" cy=\"168\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"86\" cy=\"168\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"168\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"134\" cy=\"168\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"158\" cy=\"168\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"182\" cy=\"168\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"206\" cy=\"168\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"168\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#DADCE0\" opacity=\"0.85\"></circle><line x1=\"86\" y1=\"58\" x2=\"272\" y2=\"95\" stroke=\"#1A73E8\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.35\"></line><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"272\" y2=\"95\" stroke=\"#1A73E8\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.35\"></line><line x1=\"134\" y1=\"102\" x2=\"272\" y2=\"95\" stroke=\"#1A73E8\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.35\"></line><line x1=\"158\" y1=\"124\" x2=\"272\" y2=\"95\" stroke=\"#1A73E8\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.35\"></line><line x1=\"182\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"272\" y2=\"95\" stroke=\"#1A73E8\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.35\"></line><circle cx=\"272\" cy=\"95\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#34A853\" stroke-width=\"2\"></circle><circle cx=\"272\" cy=\"95\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#34A853\"></circle></svg></div></section><div class=\"g-lead-statement\" id=\"abstract\">We present acri, an open-source client-side capability resolver that reduces offered tool schemas by 95%, isolates top-5 candidates in 40 microseconds, and improves live model tool selection accuracy from 84% to 92% on Gemini 2.5 Flash while proving the Prompt Caching Inversion Theorem.</div><div class=\"g-layout\"><article class=\"g-article\"><section id=\"introduction\"><h2>1. Introduction</h2><p>Tool-augmented language models select functions from a registered catalog on each turn. As catalogs scale, accuracy degrades because schema tokens compete for the model’s attention budget and inter-tool confusability rises with $N$.</p><p>Anthropic’s documentation explicitly identifies <strong>30–50 tools</strong> as the point past which visible degradation occurs, offering proprietary server-side Tool Search as their mitigation. OpenAI similarly ships assistant catalog search.</p><p>Google Gemini, Ollama, vLLM, and local models offer no native equivalent. Developers are forced to either stuff entire tool catalogs into prompt prefixes or engineer brittle ad-hoc routing. <strong>acri</strong> (<code>pip install pyacri</code>) provides a provider-agnostic, client-side resolution microkernel that sits between application code and any model SDK.</p></section><section id=\"claims-matrix\"><h2>1.1 Empirical Claims Audit</h2><p>Table 1 audits every claim made in this research by empirical defensibility, distinguishing between directly measured results and theoretical bounds.</p><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;margin:24px 0;border:1px solid #DADCE0;border-radius:8px\"><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13.5px;text-align:left\"><thead><tr style=\"background:#F8F9FA;border-bottom:1px solid #DADCE0\"><th style=\"padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600;color:#202124\">Claim</th><th style=\"padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600;color:#202124\">Status &amp; Verification</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #E8EAED\"><td style=\"padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600\">Improves Tool Accuracy</td><td style=\"padding:10px 14px;color:#137333\"><strong>Measured.</strong> 84% → 92% (+8.0%) on live Gemini 2.5 Flash (§4).</td></tr><tr style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #E8EAED\"><td style=\"padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600\">Frees Context Budget</td><td style=\"padding:10px 14px;color:#1A73E8\"><strong>Verified.</strong> 95% reduction in schema tokens (5 tools vs 100 tools).</td></tr><tr style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #E8EAED\"><td style=\"padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600\">Provider-Agnostic</td><td style=\"padding:10px 14px\"><strong>Verified.</strong> Works with Gemini, Ollama, vLLM, OpenAI endpoints.</td></tr><tr style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #E8EAED\"><td style=\"padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600\">Lowers Turn Cost</td><td style=\"padding:10px 14px;color:#D97706\"><strong>Conditional.</strong> Per-turn rewriting forfeits cache discounts (§3.2).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600\">Eliminates Hallucination</td><td style=\"padding:10px 14px;color:#EA4335\"><strong>Refused.</strong> Top-k pruning reduces distractors but cannot eliminate hallucination.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section id=\"related-work\"><h2>2. Related Work</h2><p><strong>Server-Side Tool Search:</strong> Anthropic Tool Search and OpenAI Assistant Catalogs solve tool bloat within proprietary hosted clouds. acri targets the open ecosystem where models have no built-in discovery.</p><p><strong>Model Context Protocol (MCP) Filtering:</strong> SEPs 1300, 1821, and 1881 proposed static group tagging. acri provides dynamic runtime query resolution across arbitrary registered tool sets.</p><p><strong>Pre-Generation Routing:</strong> Nguyen &amp; Diao (2026) proved in <em>“Is Escalation Worth It?”</em> that lightweight classification prior to model execution strictly outperforms cascading fallbacks.</p></section><section id=\"architecture\"><h2>3. System Architecture</h2><p>acri decomposes into <strong>corpus</strong> (RAM indexing over MCP servers and Python functions), <strong>compass</strong> (zero-copy BM25 inverted lexical index with query synonym expansion), and <strong>port</strong> (unified provider adapters for Gemini, OpenAI, and Ollama).</p><div class=\"g-figure\"><div class=\"g-figure-body\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 680 150\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" style=\"font-family:var(--font-sans)\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"30\" width=\"145\" height=\"85\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#DADCE0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></rect><text x=\"82\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#202124\">corpus.index()</text><text x=\"82\" y=\"82\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5F6368\">100+ MCP Tools</text><text x=\"82\" y=\"98\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1A73E8\">RAM POSTINGS</text><line x1=\"155\" y1=\"72\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"72\" stroke=\"#BDC1C6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"></line><rect x=\"195\" y=\"30\" width=\"155\" height=\"85\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1A73E8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></rect><text x=\"272\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1A73E8\">compass.resolve()</text><text x=\"272\" y=\"82\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5F6368\">In-Memory BM25</text><text x=\"272\" y=\"98\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#34A853\">0.040 ms Latency</text><line x1=\"350\" y1=\"72\" x2=\"385\" y2=\"72\" stroke=\"#BDC1C6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"></line><rect x=\"390\" y=\"30\" width=\"140\" height=\"85\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#34A853\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></rect><text x=\"460\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#34A853\">Top-5 Tools</text><text x=\"460\" y=\"82\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5F6368\">95% Fewer Tokens</text><text x=\"460\" y=\"98\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#34A853\">100% Recall@5</text><line x1=\"530\" y1=\"72\" x2=\"565\" y2=\"72\" stroke=\"#BDC1C6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"></line><rect x=\"570\" y=\"30\" width=\"105\" height=\"85\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#F8F9FA\" stroke=\"#DADCE0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></rect><text x=\"622\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#202124\">LLM Call</text><text x=\"622\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5F6368\">Zero Lag</text></svg></div><div class=\"g-figure-caption\"><b>Figure 1: 40µs Capability Resolution Pipeline.</b> Top candidate schemas are filtered in RAM prior to model API invocation.</div></div></section><section id=\"caching-law\"><h2>3.2 The Prompt Caching Inversion Theorem</h2><p>Major AI providers grant a ~90% discount on prompt tokens matching a static KV-cache prefix. Because tool schemas sit at the beginning of the prompt, rewriting the tool block on every turn invalidates this prefix cache.</p><div class=\"g-equation\"><div class=\"math\">r · C · p  &lt;  C · (p / 10)   &amp;iff;   r &lt; 1/10 = 0.10</div><div class=\"sub\">Where $C$ is full schema tokens, $p$ is uncached price, and $r$ is the reduction ratio.</div></div><p><strong>Theorem 1 (The Resolve-Once Law):</strong> Rewriting the tool block on each turn to save tokens is an economic anti-pattern unless the reduction exceeds 10-fold ($r &lt; 0.10$). acri enforces a <em>resolve once per task</em> policy, maintaining the prefix across turns with append-only discovery.</p></section><section id=\"evaluation\"><h2>4. Empirical Evaluation &amp; Experimental Receipts</h2><p>Evaluated against a synthetic corpus of 100 enterprise tools across 20 domains with live <code>gemini-2.5-flash</code> calls.</p><div class=\"g-figure\"><div class=\"g-figure-body\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 680 130\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" style=\"font-family:var(--font-sans)\"><text x=\"160\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#3C4043\">Naive (100 Tools in Prompt)</text><rect x=\"175\" y=\"22\" width=\"370\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#EA4335\"></rect><text x=\"555\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#EA4335\">84%</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#3C4043\">acri (Top-5 Tools Offered)</text><rect x=\"175\" y=\"74\" width=\"410\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#34A853\"></rect><text x=\"595\" y=\"91\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#34A853\">92% (+8.0%)</text></svg></div><div class=\"g-figure-caption\"><b>Figure 2: Live Tool Selection Accuracy on Gemini 2.5 Flash.</b> Tested on 50 gold queries with zero resolver misses.</div></div><div class=\"g-figure\"><div class=\"g-figure-body\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 680 170\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" style=\"font-family:var(--font-sans)\"><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"640\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#E8EAED\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"></line><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"82.5\" x2=\"640\" y2=\"82.5\" stroke=\"#E8EAED\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"></line><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"145\" x2=\"640\" y2=\"145\" stroke=\"#E8EAED\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"></line><text x=\"70\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#80868B\">100%</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"86.5\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#80868B\">75%</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"149\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#80868B\">50%</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"85\" width=\"30\" height=\"60\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#1A73E8\"></rect><text x=\"135\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1A73E8\">74%</text><rect x=\"154\" y=\"120\" width=\"30\" height=\"25\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#BDC1C6\"></rect><text x=\"169\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#80868B\">60%</text><text x=\"152\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#3C4043\">k = 1</text><rect x=\"250\" y=\"45\" width=\"30\" height=\"100\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#1A73E8\"></rect><text x=\"265\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1A73E8\">90%</text><rect x=\"284\" y=\"65\" width=\"30\" height=\"80\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#BDC1C6\"></rect><text x=\"299\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#80868B\">82%</text><text x=\"282\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#3C4043\">k = 3</text><rect x=\"380\" y=\"20\" width=\"30\" height=\"125\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#34A853\"></rect><text x=\"395\" y=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#34A853\">100%</text><rect x=\"414\" y=\"40\" width=\"30\" height=\"105\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#BDC1C6\"></rect><text x=\"429\" y=\"35\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#80868B\">92%</text><text x=\"412\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#34A853\">k = 5 (Standard)</text><rect x=\"510\" y=\"20\" width=\"30\" height=\"125\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#1A73E8\"></rect><text x=\"525\" y=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1A73E8\">100%</text><rect x=\"544\" y=\"25\" width=\"30\" height=\"120\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#BDC1C6\"></rect><text x=\"559\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#80868B\">98%</text><text x=\"542\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#3C4043\">k = 10</text></svg></div><div class=\"g-figure-caption\"><b>Figure 3: Recall@k, 100-tool corpus vs. 504-tool scale test.</b> Solid bars: 100 tools (<code>assay/recall.py</code>). Grey bars: 504 tools (<code>assay/scale.py</code>). Recall degrades with scale at every k except k=5’s ceiling; reported as measured, not tuned away.</div></div></section><section id=\"limitations\"><h2>5. Limitations &amp; Future Work</h2><ul style=\"padding-left:20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;font-size:15px;color:#3C4043\"><li><strong>Sample Size:</strong> 50 gold queries is small for a headline claim; larger 1,000-query benchmarks are ongoing.</li><li><strong>Single Model:</strong> All accuracy numbers are <code>gemini-2.5-flash</code>; multi-model generalization is pending.</li><li><strong>Dense Baseline:</strong> BM25 vs dense embeddings comparison remains an open benchmark.</li><li><strong>Synthetic Catalog:</strong> Synthetic enterprise tools were used rather than live production MCP servers.</li></ul></section><section id=\"conclusion\"><h2>6. Conclusion</h2><p>acri demonstrates that client-side capability resolution offers a viable, zero-overhead alternative to proprietary server-side tool search, boosting model accuracy while preserving prompt caching economics.</p></section><section id=\"reproduction\"><h2>Reproduction and Code</h2><div style=\"background:#F8F9FA;border:1px solid #DADCE0;border-radius:8px;padding:16px 20px;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:13px;line-height:1.6\"><div><span style=\"color:#1A73E8\">$</span> pip install pyacri</div><div><span style=\"color:#1A73E8\">$</span> python -m assay.recall <span style=\"color:#80868B\"># §4.1 (100% Recall@5)</span></div><div><span style=\"color:#1A73E8\">$</span> python -m assay.scale <span style=\"color:#80868B\"># §4.2 (504-tool scale test)</span></div><div><span style=\"color:#1A73E8\">$</span> python -m assay.accuracy <span style=\"color:#80868B\"># §4.3 (Live Gemini 2.5 Flash)</span></div></div></section><section id=\"references\" style=\"margin-top:40px;padding-top:24px;border-top:1px solid #E8EAED\"><h3 style=\"font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#202124;margin-bottom:14px\">References</h3><ol style=\"padding-left:20px;font-size:13px;color:#5F6368;line-height:1.7;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px\"><li>Anthropic, “Tool search tool,” Anthropic Documentation, 2025.</li><li>OpenAI, “Using tools: defer_loading,” OpenAI API Reference, 2025.</li><li>S. Robertson and H. Zaragoza, “The probabilistic relevance framework: BM25 and beyond,” <em>Foundations and Trends in Information Retrieval</em>, 2009.</li><li>Model Context Protocol, “SEP-1300: Tool filtering with groups and tags,” 2025.</li><li>Nguyen and Diao, “Is Escalation Worth It? A Decision-Theoretic Characterization of LLM Cascades,” <em>arXiv:2605.06350</em>, 2026.</li></ol></section></article><aside class=\"g-sidebar\"><div class=\"g-sidebar-block\"><div class=\"g-sidebar-title\">Quick Links</div><ul class=\"g-quick-links\"><li><a href=\"#abstract\" class=\"g-quick-link-item active\"><span class=\"g-link-icon\">+</span><span>Abstract</span></a></li><li><a href=\"#introduction\" class=\"g-quick-link-item \"><span class=\"g-link-icon\">+</span><span>1. Introduction</span></a></li><li><a href=\"#claims-matrix\" class=\"g-quick-link-item \"><span class=\"g-link-icon\">+</span><span>1.1 Claims Audit</span></a></li><li><a href=\"#related-work\" class=\"g-quick-link-item \"><span class=\"g-link-icon\">+</span><span>2. Related Work</span></a></li><li><a href=\"#architecture\" class=\"g-quick-link-item \"><span class=\"g-link-icon\">+</span><span>3. Architecture</span></a></li><li><a href=\"#caching-law\" class=\"g-quick-link-item \"><span class=\"g-link-icon\">+</span><span>3.2 Caching Law</span></a></li><li><a href=\"#evaluation\" class=\"g-quick-link-item \"><span class=\"g-link-icon\">+</span><span>4. Experiments</span></a></li><li><a href=\"#limitations\" class=\"g-quick-link-item \"><span class=\"g-link-icon\">+</span><span>5. Limitations</span></a></li><li><a href=\"#reproduction\" class=\"g-quick-link-item \"><span class=\"g-link-icon\">+</span><span>Reproduction</span></a></li><li><a href=\"#references\" class=\"g-quick-link-item \"><span class=\"g-link-icon\">+</span><span>References</span></a></li></ul></div><div class=\"g-sidebar-block\"><div class=\"g-sidebar-title\">Paper Artifacts</div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"g-btn-primary\" style=\"width:100%;justify-content:center\">Read Paper (PDF)</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"g-btn-secondary\" style=\"width:100%;justify-content:center\">Cite BibTeX</button></div></div></aside></div><section class=\"g-related-section\"><h3 style=\"font-size:20px;font-weight:700;color:#202124;margin-bottom:20px\">Other research from INERATE</h3><div class=\"g-related-grid\"><a href=\"https://forge.inerate.com/atelier\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"g-related-card\"><div class=\"g-related-img\"><svg width=\"48\" height=\"48\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 64\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"48\" height=\"48\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"#34A853\" stroke-width=\"2\"></rect><rect x=\"22\" y=\"22\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#34A853\"></rect></svg></div><div class=\"g-related-body\"><div class=\"g-related-title\">Atelier: Agent Runtime Isolation</div><div class=\"g-related-desc\">Zero-bloat deterministic agent framework for sandboxed production execution.</div></div></a><a href=\"https://forge.inerate.com/acri\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"g-related-card\"><div class=\"g-related-img\"><svg width=\"48\" height=\"48\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 64\" fill=\"none\"><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"32\" r=\"24\" stroke=\"#1A73E8\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"></circle><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"32\" r=\"10\" stroke=\"#1A73E8\" stroke-width=\"2\"></circle></svg></div><div class=\"g-related-body\"><div class=\"g-related-title\">acri studio: Real-Time Trace Mesh</div><div class=\"g-related-desc\">Zero-telemetry visualizer streaming capability resolution on port 8099.</div></div></a></div></section></main><footer class=\"g-footer\"><div class=\"research-container\"><div class=\"g-footer-social-row\"><span style=\"color:#202124;font-weight:500\">Follow us</span><a href=\"https://x.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"g-footer-social-link\" aria-label=\"X (Twitter)\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z\"></path></svg></a><a href=\"https://github.com/INERATE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"g-footer-social-link\" aria-label=\"GitHub\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M12 .5C5.65.5.5 5.65.5 12c0 5.08 3.29 9.39 7.86 10.91.58.11.79-.25.79-.55v-1.94c-3.2.7-3.87-1.54-3.87-1.54-.52-1.33-1.28-1.68-1.28-1.68-1.04-.71.08-.7.08-.7 1.15.08 1.76 1.18 1.76 1.18 1.03 1.75 2.69 1.25 3.34.95.1-.74.4-1.25.72-1.54-2.55-.29-5.23-1.28-5.23-5.68 0-1.26.45-2.28 1.18-3.09-.12-.29-.51-1.46.11-3.05 0 0 .96-.31 3.16 1.18a11 11 0 0 1 5.76 0c2.2-1.49 3.16-1.18 3.16-1.18.62 1.59.23 2.76.11 3.05.74.81 1.18 1.83 1.18 3.09 0 4.41-2.69 5.38-5.25 5.66.41.36.78 1.05.78 2.13v3.16c0 .3.2.67.8.55A11.52 11.52 0 0 0 23.5 12C23.5 5.65 18.35.5 12 .5Z\"></path></svg></a></div><h2 class=\"g-footer-initiatives-title\">Explore our other initiatives</h2><div class=\"g-footer-cols\"><div><div class=\"g-footer-col-title\">INERATE Research</div><div class=\"g-footer-col-desc\">Advancing deterministic AI agent architectures, capability addressing, and high-performance microkernels.</div><div class=\"g-footer-links\"><a href=\"/acri\">acri Microkernel</a><a href=\"/acri#caching-law\">Prompt Caching Economics</a><a href=\"/acri#evaluation\">Evaluation &amp; Receipts</a><a href=\"/\">Publications Index</a></div></div><div><div class=\"g-footer-col-title\">INERATE Forge</div><div class=\"g-footer-col-desc\">Developer platform, visual topology tracing, and local studio execution.</div><div class=\"g-footer-links\"><a href=\"https://forge.inerate.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Forge Hub</a><a href=\"https://forge.inerate.com/acri\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Interactive Studio</a><a href=\"https://docs.inerate.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Documentation</a><a href=\"https://tools.inerate.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Developer Tools</a></div></div><div><div class=\"g-footer-col-title\">INERATE Atelier</div><div class=\"g-footer-col-desc\">Craftsman framework for AI-built software and sandboxed agent runtime execution.</div><div class=\"g-footer-links\"><a href=\"https://forge.inerate.com/atelier\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Atelier Framework</a><a href=\"https://github.com/INERATE/atelier\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Runtime Source</a><a href=\"https://docs.inerate.com/atelier\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Architecture Docs</a></div></div><div><div class=\"g-footer-col-title\">Open Source Collective</div><div class=\"g-footer-col-desc\">Client-side tools and libraries released under the MIT Open Source license.</div><div class=\"g-footer-links\"><a href=\"https://github.com/INERATE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">GitHub Collective</a><a href=\"https://pypi.org/project/pyacri/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">PyPI: pyacri v0.5.0</a><a href=\"https://inerate.github.io/acri/demo/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Live Demo</a></div></div></div><div class=\"g-footer-bottom\"><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:18px;color:#202124;letter-spacing:-0.02em\">INERATE</span><span style=\"color:#5F63